          "description": "SHA-256 of the **stored** bytes, lowercase hex, as the writer computed it. It names the bytes that travel, which is what lets a client tell a block it already holds from one it has to fetch. Reading a container checks the shape of this field and nothing more: the digest is not recomputed, so it identifies a block rather than attesting to it. What guards a decode is the block's own framing."
